WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:03.919
Get ready for a bit of a bummer, true believers.

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:08.160
Mighty Marvel might be running like a well-oiled
machine, but according to writer/director

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.190
James Gunn, it's going to take a little longer
than we might like for that machine to pump

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.740
out Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:19.170
In a recent exchange with a fan on Instagram,
Gunn revealed that the three-quel for the

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:24.869
spacefaring team of misfits won't start filming
for, quote, "another year or so."

00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:29.279
The news isn't entirely unexpected, as we've
known for quite some time that Gunn will have

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:33.880
a bit of work to wrap up for the Distinguished
Competition before he can turn his attention

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.270
to Guardians 3.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:39.690
As you may recall, the director was temporarily
fired from the Marvel flick due to a kerfuffle

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:45.250
over some nearly decade-old tweets in 2018;
he was reinstated in March 2019, but in the

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:50.080
meantime, he had taken a gig with Warner Bros.
and DC Films writing and directing the soft

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.990
reboot The Suicide Squad.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:57.310
Marvel, in no hurry to rush Guardians 3 to
the screen with its slate already chock full,

00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:01.810
allowed Gunn to finish up his work on the
DC film before returning.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:06.110
According to CBR, Gunn has said that shooting
on The Suicide Squad is only about two-thirds

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:11.940
complete as recently as December 18; assuming
the flick sticks to its production schedule,

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:16.740
it's likely to wrap by February or so, at
which point Gunn will be knee-deep in the

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.680
post-production process for another several
months.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:24.850
Of course, nobody would blame Gunn if he wanted
to cool his jets for just awhile before taking

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:29.540
on another massive comic book film, so his
stated time frame for Guardians 3 to begin

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.920
production sounds just about right.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.120
However, assuming that shooting does indeed
get underway in late 2020, we can infer that

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.110
we've got a pretty damn long wait before the
flick actually hits theaters.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:46.820
Consider that The Suicide Squad has been slotted
for release on August 6, 2021; this means

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:51.200
that from wrap to release, we're looking at
a period of about 16 months.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:56.280
If Guardians 3 has a fairly typical 3-4 month
shoot, then it'll wrap right around March

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:02.140
or April of 2021 and if it has a comparable
post-production schedule, the very earliest

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:06.880
we could expect to see it hit screens is July
or August of 2022.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:12.120
The sequel to Black Panther is already slated
for release on May 6 of that year, and Marvel

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:17.470
has a number of other films that might shoulder
their way into its two remaining 2022 slots,

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.870
including Blade and the third installment
in the Ant-Man series.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:26.560
It follows, then, that Guardians of the Galaxy
Vol. 3 may not even appear in theaters until

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.900
sometime in 2023 — more than three years
from now.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.730
Guess we'll all just have to pop into hibernation
for a bit, huh?

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:39.740
"Do one of those on me!"

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:43.730
"Sleeeep."

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:48.440
While the MCU's feature schedule is all sewn
up through Black Panther 2, there are still

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:53.340
a number of flicks in addition to those already
mentioned that don't yet have release dates.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:59.260
Perhaps the most high-profile is Captain Marvel
2, the sequel to the 2019 billion-dollar smash

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:04.380
which will see Brie Larson reprise her role
as the uber-powerful cosmic hero.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:09.260
Also heavily rumored to be in active development
is Nova, a solo vehicle for the even more

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:13.130
powerful hero who should have an intimate
connection to the Guardians.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:18.220
Essentially Marvel's answer to DC's Green
Lantern, the "man called Nova" is Richard

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:23.459
Rider, an Earthling imbued with the power
of the entire Nova Corps, the cosmically-powered

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:25.989
armed forces of the planet Xandar.

00:03:25.989 --> 00:03:30.800
As you may recall, Xandar came under threat
by the Infinity Stone-wielding Ronan the Accuser

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.849
in the first Guardians film.

00:03:32.849 --> 00:03:38.190
In the comics, Rider is chosen at random by
the Xandarian Rhomann Dey to house the power

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.129
of the Nova Corps after the planet's destruction.

00:03:41.129 --> 00:03:46.180
Rider is also imbued with the "Xandarian Worldmind"
basically the collective knowledge of the

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:48.180
entire Xandarian race.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:53.790
That's right, Nova is basically the most robust
supercomputer one can imagine... a supercomputer

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:56.470
that can punch a planet out of its orbit.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:04:01.670
King Geek and Marvel mastermind Kevin Feige
has also recently teased that there is indeed

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:06.200
another team-up film on the way, although
he characteristically held back any relevant

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.530
details.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:12.590
Since Marvel's "phases" are running a bit
shorter now Phase 4 is taking place over 2020

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:19.590
and 2021, with Phase 5 taking up 2022 and
2023 it seems likely that we'll be getting

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:24.210
an official announcement on this sometime
pretty soon, unless it gets pushed off until

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.210
Phase 6.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:30.150
At any rate, we'll just have to wait until
Feige and company see their way clear to cluing

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:36.080
us in on when we can expect the Guardians
of the Galaxy, Blade, Captain Marvel, Ant-Man

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:40.569
and the Wasp, Nova, and The Avengers whatever
the heck the next iteration of that team will

00:04:40.569 --> 00:04:43.069
look like to return to theaters.

00:04:43.069 --> 00:04:47.870
Of course, we'll be all over any breaking
Marvel news, and we'll be sure to keep you

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.020
informed.

